1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
He rose from an artillery officer

2
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:04,870
to become the most feared
ruler in Europe.

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,230
Napoleon Bonaparte crowned himself

4
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:10,090
Emperor of the French
in 1804.

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,940
His armies won
extraordinary victories,

6
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:15,550
and his empire
reshaped the continent.

7
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,990
But Napoleon wanted more.

8
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:20,510
In 1812, he invaded Russia

9
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,040
with a vast
multinational army.

10
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,610
He reached Moscow,

11
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:27,090
only to find much of the city
burning.

12
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,030
Then came the retreat.

13
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:31,680
Hunger, disease, exhaustion,

14
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:34,740
and bitter cold
devastated his forces.

15
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:36,540
His enemies united.

16
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:40,080
In 1814, Napoleon abdicated

17
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:41,930
and was exiled to Elba.

18
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,680
He returned the following year

19
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,650
for one final gamble.

20
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:48,570
At Waterloo,
his army was defeated.

21
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:52,700
This time, exile meant
a remote island in the Atlantic:

22
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:53,830
Saint Helena.

23
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:57,070
Napoleon died there
in 1821.

24
00:00:57,690 --> 00:01:00,020
He conquered kingdoms,
changed Europe,

25
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:02,060
and became a legend.

26
00:01:02,330 --> 00:01:03,400
But he could not conquer

27
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:06,160
the consequences
of his own ambition.

